{
  "comment": "The Prism as a product, after afflom/prism-devrel's Architecture (ISO/IEC/IEEE 42010 stakeholders, concerns, viewpoints), Users (ISO 9241-11 goals and usability measures) and Features (journeys). It grows one journey at a time: a journey is 'works' only once its walk passes for a synthetic person, and from then on every PR and every live deploy must keep it working. tools/product/gate.py checks this record against the surface, the coherence registry and the walks; test/product/screen.test.mjs keeps the system view off the screen; test/product/journeys.test.mjs walks every journey. Nothing here is ever shown on the page. Journeys and facets are kept one file each under journeys/ and facets/ (read by tools/specs/record.py), so parallel changes never collide.",
  "stakeholders": [
    {
      "key": "person",
      "concerns": [
        "my day is there without setting anything up",
        "nothing I owe or am owed slips",
        "each thing that needs me takes one gesture",
        "what I jot down lands in the right place",
        "my questions are answered with where the answer came from",
        "I am left alone when I ask for quiet",
        "I never manage the machinery",
        "nothing about me leaves my device without my say"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "builder",
      "concerns": [
        "every change keeps every working journey working",
        "the journey furthest from its target is built next",
        "every part of the back end serves a journey"
      ]
    }
  ],
